Subject: [PATCH] sycl: MoE MMVQ for 2..8 tokens, fused gate + up + GLU and ADD_ID biases

Local port of CUDA's mul_mat_vec_q with ids and fusion args to the MoE MMVQ kernels (plain and
reorder layout), through one optional ggml_sycl_moe_mmvq_ext:

- Tokens: the fused MoE path took one token; a speculative-decoding verify or parallel slots of 2..8
  tokens went to the grouped XMX GEMM (mostly empty 32-column tiles) or the per-expert loop. The grid
  now spans tokens x expert slots. The cap per type is CUDA's RDNA3 table (4 for the k-quants and
  IQ2 / IQ3, 6 for IQ1 / IQ4, else 8), unmeasured on Intel; GGML_SYCL_MMID_MMVQ_MAX_TOKENS overrides it.
- {MUL_MAT_ID gate, MUL_MAT_ID up, GLU}, optionally with the ADD_ID bias of each lane (gpt-oss): one
  launch reads the activation once and writes glu(gate . y [+ gate bias], up . y [+ up bias]) for
  SWIGLU, GEGLU, SWIGLU_OAI and SWIGLU_CLAMP. Gate and up must share type, shape and layout. The
  plain-layout q3_K kernel with the gate spills on acm-g10 and keeps two launches.
- A lone MUL_MAT_ID + ADD_ID (gpt-oss's down projection) adds the bias in the store.

graph_optimize keeps the routing ids alive until the fused output, which the kernels read while writing.

